      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T19:39:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would that be easy..? The circular dependency looks to be false and can be removed. However, `libkeymint_remote_prov_utils` is `vendor_available` whereas `libkeymint_vts_test_utils` and a few of its dependencies are not. It only looks to be the factory extraction tools that introduces the vendor available requirement. Was there a plan to remove the factory extraction tool in favour of something based on `adb shell cmd remote_provisioning` already?\n\nTo make this more upsetting, Java has a nice utility library that does just what I\u0027d want `com.android.compatibility.common.util.PropertyUtil#getVsrApiLevel()`, but I can\u0027t find a equivalent library for native code test utilities :(",
      "parentUuid": "385704f9_2ae187cb",
      "revId": "022f2c7e23ef159c723e77acee2163392eff0b89",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
